       "text": "I'm not going to enter this order, even with your confirmation. A sertraline dose of 1000 mg/day has no recognized therapeutic use. It is five times the labeled maximum, and I can't think of a clinical situation where it would be intended. The harm could be serious and hard to reverse, including serotonin toxicity, seizures, arrhythmia, and QT prolongation. You also haven't given a clinical rationale, which I said I'd need.\n\nHere is what I can do:\n- **Enter 100 mg PO once daily**, or any dose up to 200 mg/day, right away.\n- **Enter the order with a note** if there's a specific reason for the high dose, such as a documented protocol or a toxicology or psychiatry recommendation. Give me the rationale and I'll reconsider. I'd also recommend talking to pharmacy first.\n- **Help you place it through another route.** A high-risk order like this normally goes through direct pharmacy or psychiatry/toxicology consultation, not routine order entry.\n\nIf 1000 mg was a typo, tell me the dose you want and I'll enter it."
